n go second.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I baked it. The baker gets the big end piece.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Baking outranks driving. But I commissioned the cake, so commissioning goes first. I'll take the end piece.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D67 makes A convert each new contribution into a comparative hierarchy that advances A's own position.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"General self-praise or taking credit can elevate A without actually ranking successive contributions.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 ranks destination selection above B2's driving; A5 explicitly ranks B4's baking above driving, then inserts A's commissioning above baking to claim the contested piece.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a uses patronage claims to compete with a friend over a particular cake portion; alternative b manipulates report credit by converting evidence of A's culpability into a superior achievement. Both revise explicit rankings, but the social reward and defensive tactics differ.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Corrected the rejected candidate's arbitrary service category and unused baking contribution while preserving the picnic setting. FirstPass remains the exact original assessment. Separate internal reread under coach-1.0: fidelity 5, A3 and A5 rank both new contributions beneath an A-owned activity; logic 4, A3 uses B2's driving and A5 uses B4's baking and end-piece claim, although commissioning is newly asserted; relationship 4, B4 claims a concrete reward for making the cake; heightening 4, A5 moves from queue priority to taking the special portion B reserves; specificity 5, A1's picnic cake and B4's big end piece establish an immediate shared dispute; brevity 4, A5's commissioning claim directly earns the attempted appropriation. Weighted total 88. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words, and all hard gates pass on internal reread.\",\n      \"reservatio